<h2 id="h-what-whitetail-maxx-rth-is-built-to-do">What the Bear Whitetail Maxx RTH Is Built to Do</h2>
<p>As the name says, the Whitetail Maxx is aimed squarely at deer hunters. Most whitetail shots happen inside 30 or 40 yards, often from an elevated stand or a cramped blind. That calls for a bow that is short enough to maneuver, quiet enough not to spook deer and forgiving enough to shoot well when you are cold, cramped and excited.</p>
<p>The 31-inch frame is the key. It swings easily around stand straps and tree limbs, and it fits inside a ground blind without the limbs knocking against the roof. A longer bow can feel steadier on long range shots, but for typical whitetail distances, a 31-inch bow is a practical sweet spot.</p>

<h2 id="h-draw-cycle-let-off-and-mechanical-efficiency">Draw Cycle, Let-Off and Draw Weight</h2>
<p>The Whitetail Maxx offers two draw weight ranges: 45&ndash;60 lb and 55&ndash;70 lb. Each can be backed off about 15 pounds from its peak, which makes it easy to start lighter and build strength over the off-season.</p>
