<p>With up to 90% let-off, the holding weight at full draw drops to a small fraction of peak weight. That matters in the woods. When a buck stops behind a tree with your bow drawn, high let-off lets you hold longer without shaking. Some shooters prefer a little more holding weight for a firmer feel, which is why the 80% figure you may see on some listings is worth noting.</p>
