<h2 id="h-durability-wear-and-long-term-use">Durability, Wear and Long-Term Use</h2>
<p>Like any compound bow, the Whitetail Maxx lasts longer with simple care:</p>
<ol class="steps">
  <li>Wax the string and cables every few weeks of regular shooting.</li>
  <li>Check accessory screws on the sight, rest, quiver and stabilizer before each hunt.</li>
  <li>Inspect the Whisker Biscuit bristles for wear and replace the insert when it loosens.</li>
  <li>Never dry-fire the bow.</li>
  <li>Store it in a padded case away from heat and moisture.</li>
</ol>
<p>Expect to replace strings and cables after a few seasons depending on how much you shoot. At Better Outdoors we recommend having a pro shop check cam timing and peep alignment at the same time.</p>

